<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Converting degrees to radians</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Convert the angle \({@angdeg@}^\circ\) to radians.</p>
<div>radians \(=\)  [[input:ans1]]  [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p><i> Type \(\pi\) as <code>pi</code>, and use <code>*</code> for multiplication and <code>/</code> for division. </i></p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>
<p><strong>Step 1: use the conversion fact.</strong> A half-turn is \(180^\circ\), which is \(\pi\) radians:</p>
\[ 180^\circ = \pi \text{ radians}, \qquad\text{so}\qquad 1^\circ = \frac{\pi}{180} \text{ radians}. \]

<p><strong>Step 2: multiply by \(\dfrac{\pi}{180}\).</strong> To change degrees to radians, multiply the angle by \(\dfrac{\pi}{180}\):</p>
\[ {@angdeg@}^\circ = {@angdeg@} \times \frac{\pi}{180} = \frac{{@angdeg@}\pi}{180}. \]

<p><strong>Step 3: simplify the fraction.</strong> The highest common factor of \({@angdeg@}\) and \(180\) is \({@hcf@}\). Divide the top and the bottom by \({@hcf@}\):</p>
\[ \frac{{@angdeg@}\pi}{180} = \frac{{@angdeg@} \div {@hcf@}}{180 \div {@hcf@}}\,\pi = {@ta1@}. \]
<div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="Circle showing the angle {#angdeg#} degrees measured anticlockwise from the positive x-axis.">
[[jsxgraph width="300px" height="300px"]]
(function() {
  var A = {#angdeg#}, num = {#nn#}, den = {#dd#};
  var b = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox:[-1.5, 1.5, 1.5, -1.5], axis:false, grid:false,
      keepaspectratio:true, showNavigation:false, showCopyright:false});
  b.create('arrow', [[-1.4, 0], [1.45, 0]], {strokeColor:'#444', fixed:true, highlight:false});
  b.create('arrow', [[0, -1.4], [0, 1.45]], {strokeColor:'#444', fixed:true, highlight:false});
  b.create('circle', [[0, 0], 1], {strokeColor:'#90a4ae', strokeWidth:1.5, fixed:true, highlight:false});
  var O = b.create('point', [0, 0], {visible:false, fixed:true});
  var X = b.create('point', [1, 0], {visible:false, fixed:true});
  var r = A*Math.PI/180;
  var P = b.create('point', [Math.cos(r), Math.sin(r)], {name:'', size:3, color:'#c62828', fixed:true});
  b.create('segment', [O, X], {strokeColor:'#c62828', strokeWidth:2, fixed:true});
  b.create('segment', [O, P], {strokeColor:'#c62828', strokeWidth:2, fixed:true});
  var lab = (num === 1 ? '' : num) + 'π' + '/' + den;
  b.create('angle', [X, O, P], {radius:0.35, name:A + '° = ' + lab, fillColor:'#ffb74d', fillOpacity:0.35,
      strokeColor:'#ef6c00', fixed:true, label:{color:'#ef6c00', fontSize:13}});
})();
[[/jsxgraph]]
</div>
<p><strong>Final answer:</strong> \({@angdeg@}^\circ = {@ta1@}\) radians.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
